\subsection{Research attempt}
\paragraph{Model, date and investigated scope.}
OpenAI GPT-6 Astra (configured model \texttt{gpt-6-astra}), ultra reasoning; generated 11 October 2026. Explicit positive cylinder functional with no representing probability measure on l2; tests a support criterion, not the general existence/determinacy programme.

\paragraph{Sources and literature check.}
Read the supplied definition, catalogue wording, source qualifications and reference entries for 30003435. The historical source/context and inherited status are retained; no fresh literature or novelty certification is claimed. No external theorem is used without proof in this attempt; explicit model assumptions are distinguished from facts about the source model.

\paragraph{Cylinder positivity versus support.} The qualification in [S2] leaves the configuration topology open. I test the concrete choice \(K=\ell^2(\mathbb N;\mathbb R)\), with coordinate polynomials, rather than claim a criterion for all field spaces. For a polynomial \(p\) depending on its first \(N\) coordinates put
\[
 L(p)=2^{-N}\sum_{\epsilon\in\{-1,1\}^N}p(\epsilon).
\]
Adding unused coordinates duplicates summands and leaves this value unchanged, so this defines one normalized functional on all cylinder polynomials. It is positive on squares and indeed on every polynomial pointwise nonnegative on \(K\): every finite sign vector extends to a point of \(K\) by adding zeros. Thus even positivity on all such nonnegative cylinder polynomials holds.
\paragraph{Obstruction.} Suppose a countably additive probability measure \(\mu\) on \(K\), with measurable coordinates, represented \(L\). For each \(n\),
\[
 \int_K(x_n^2-1)^2\,d\mu=L((x_n^2-1)^2)=0.
\]
Nonnegativity forces \(x_n^2=1\) almost surely. The intersection of these countably many probability-one sets still has measure one, but is empty in \(\ell^2\), since then \(\sum_nx_n^2=\infty\). This contradiction needs neither a moment-determinacy theorem nor an infinite product-measure construction.
\paragraph{Audit and gap.} Finite-dimensional marginals are legitimate compactly supported measures and mutually consistent. The failure is specifically concentration on the proposed infinite-dimensional configuration space; it is not failure of those marginals. This elementary countercheck rules out deriving the requested support theorem from cylinder positivity alone. No existence/determinacy/support criterion for the source's unspecified field spaces is proved, and no novelty claim is made.

\paragraph{Verification and adversarial audit.}
Checked consistency under added coordinates, positivity on all cylinder polynomials nonnegative on l2, and the countable probability-one intersection contradiction. This is a GPT-6 Astra Ultra self-audit, not independent human verification. Prompt A drafting followed by prompt B scope/dependency/boundary self-audit. Checked consistency under added coordinates, positivity on all cylinder polynomials nonnegative on l2, and the countable probability-one intersection contradiction. The remaining gap is: Identify and prove topology-sensitive tightness/support hypotheses for the actual field configuration space. Unresolved status and zero original-target completion are retained.

Coordinator checked consistency of the finite sign marginals, positivity on l2-nonnegative cylinder polynomials, and the countable full-measure intersection contradiction. This is a support countercheck, not a field-space moment theorem. This additional check was model-assisted, not independent human verification.

\paragraph{Tools, process and contributions.}
Python 3 and local file-reading/writing tools for manuscript serialization and structural checks; mathematical calculations were symbolic reasoning, with no numerical experiment or theorem prover. Contribution prompt A was followed by prompt B. GPT-6 Astra with ultra reasoning drafted the research and performed its stated self-audit; any additional coordinator contribution is identified in the verification and audit. A GPT-6-based Codex coordinator assembled the manuscript and checked repository integration; its exact variant and reasoning configuration were not exposed. No human mathematical contribution, independent human proof check or formal proof certification is supplied. Complete derivations and the consulted source references are included here; private reasoning transcripts are not published.

\paragraph{Final status and first remaining gap.}
\textbf{UNRESOLVED}. Identify and prove topology-sensitive tightness/support hypotheses for the actual field configuration space.

